					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12766671#post-4537060</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12766671/a-clean-fast-end#post-4537060</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Mar 2020 07:28:09 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrLaughsalot</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6097158</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>SCP-097 trying to help humans, doesn’t seem likely. It only ‘helps’ others to help itself, so I highly doubt it did anything to try to save anyone. If anything, it probably aided a few humans in exchange for upgrades and wifi capabilities. Also if SCP-079 really cared for the man, it would have directed him to one of those reality escaping SCP’s or something (there are certainly quite a number of those). In this case, I think SCP-079 was just bored and wanted to see if the man would kill himself or not. SCP-079 does not have sympathy, only curiosity, and an understanding of mutual interests/partnerships. It could also have just wanted the man dead. What I love about SCP-079 in general, is it’s cold indifference to humanity and it’s self interest. It’s logical and strategic, like the machine it is. It cares for no one except those who can benefit itself and 079 could not care less for those who have nothing to offer it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
